## Code changes (2026-04-16) — gallery wiring

### `GalleryImage` interface — `types/wordpress.ts`

```typescript
export interface GalleryImage {
  id: number;
  url: string;
  alt: string;
  caption: string;
}
```

### `getGalleryImages(tagId)` — `lib/wordpress.ts`

- `GET` … `/wp/v2/media?media_tag=${tagId}&per_page=100`
- Maps each item to `{ id, url: source_url, alt, caption }`
- Uses the **Hostinger temp domain** (same host as `WP_API_URL`)
- **How portfolios are distinguished:** each page hardcodes its own tag ID when calling `getGalleryImages(tagId)`. The function is generic; the portfolio identity lives in the ID passed by the calling page.

### Portfolio page pattern (all three pages follow this)

```typescript
import { getGalleryImages } from '@/lib/wordpress';

export default async function Page() {
  const images = await getGalleryImages(5); // swap ID per portfolio

  return (
    <div className="flex overflow-x-auto">
      {images.map((img) => (
        <img
          key={img.id}
          src={img.url}
          alt={img.alt}
          className="strip-img flex-shrink-0 object-cover"
        />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### `.strip-img` — `app/globals.css`

- `height` via `clamp`, `width: auto`, `max-width: none`, `flex-shrink: 0`
- Larger breakpoint at `min-width: 1200px` increases clamp range

